        However the maps did not turn out as expected. Imagine this, from a top down view, you took a picture of the room you are in and put it on the paper. You then rotate 90 degrees and do the same. You do this twice more so you end up with 4 pictures of the same room. However, instead of orientating them and laying on top of each other. You lay them perpendicular with respect to the previous. This is what happend with our snapshots, they were saved with respect to the local waypoint frame, thus offsetting 90 degrees after each turn. 
